## 6. Distributed FastPath, Caching & Concurrency Mechanics

### 6.1 Redis Key Registry & Lifecycle Matrix
| Key Pattern | Redis Type | TTL | Purpose | Invalidation Trigger |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `auth:user:session:{tokenHash}` | Hash | 86400s (24h) | Fast session lookup & identity caching | Explicit logout, password reset |
| `rl:ip:{ipAddress}:{windowMinute}` | Integer | 60s | Ingress rate limiting (max 100 req/min) | Automatic expiration |
| `lock:user:login:{userId}` | String | 10s | Distributed mutex preventing login race condition | Atomic release on completion |
| `mfa:challenge:{userId}` | String | 300s (5m) | Ephemeral OTP challenge verification | Verified or expired |

### 6.2 Atomic Distributed Lock Lua Scripts
\`\`\`lua
-- Release Lock Script (Atomic release if token matches)
-- KEYS[1]: lock key (e.g. lock:user:login:123)
-- ARGV[1]: lock token UUID
if redis.call('get', KEYS[1]) == ARGV[1] then
    return redis.call('del', KEYS[1])
else
    return 0
end
\`\`\`

